WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>An unknown frontier</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>On the map painted by my heart</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>When I open the door, the path goes on</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>I'm kicking up dust as I</i>
<i>start running to your town</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Along a route where earth and sky meet</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Riding the rushing southern wind</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Slicing through the wind</i>
<i>dyed blue by the sky</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>I'm rushing out with my whole heart</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Shooting past the midday moon</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Towards a world different</i>
<i>from what we've known before</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>I will keep on running through to the end</i>

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>However far</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.544
Balance.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:10.172
We will be arriving at the base shortly.

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:13.884
What's important is balance.
For both people and countries.

00:02:13.884 --> 00:02:14.718
Sir?

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:17.179
Leaning too far to one side is a no-no!

00:02:17.179 --> 00:02:18.847
A big no-no!

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:20.682
If you lose your balance...

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.603
...something like<i> that </i>happens.

00:02:24.603 --> 00:02:27.606
The most important thing is
to maintain balance on both sides.

00:02:27.606 --> 00:02:30.567
For the sake of our business, as well.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.194
Are you talking about
North and South China, sir?

00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:36.198
Now then, it's almost time
for our little meeting with Yollan.

00:02:36.198 --> 00:02:37.241
Yollan?

00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:39.576
You don't know? How lame.

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:41.912
I'm talkin' about Yu Lan!

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:45.207
What do you intend to do with
the corpse after you've retrieved it?

00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:48.043
The body of a pretty young girl, huh?

00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:50.629
I'm sure there are plenty
of ways it can be put to use.

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:55.634
"His Problem"

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:11.900
"Hey, you want somethin'?"

00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:16.947
You're not a local, are you?

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:20.117
Are you Korean? Japanese?

00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:22.619
I don't have a homeland.

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:23.912
Huh?

00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:31.253
Well if you don't have any business here,
get lost. I'm busy right now.

00:03:32.546 --> 00:03:33.672
Are you evacuating?

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:35.465
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:37.134 --> 00:03:38.635
"Hurry up, Dear!"

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:39.970
"Shut up!"

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:44.641
I'll have this.

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:45.934
I'm in the middle of something.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:46.643
"Ready yet?"

00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:47.811
"I'll be right there!"

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.354
Please let me buy this, sir.

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:52.399
Who cares about that?
Just go ahead and take it!

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:55.485
You should get the hell out of here, too,
unless you wanna die!

00:04:03.327 --> 00:04:04.745
Die?

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.915
That might be a good idea.

00:04:07.915 --> 00:04:11.919
"Hunter Cleaning Co., Ltd."

00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:24.723
Uruz 9 to All.

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:27.017
We are now going to investigate Point 28.

00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:28.977
If you do not receive any contact
from us within 15 minutes,

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:30.646
tighten the search perimeter.

00:04:30.646 --> 00:04:32.606
Uruz 2, roger.

00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:36.026
Wangfu HQ, roger. Be careful out there.

00:04:37.986 --> 00:04:39.696
What's wrong, Corporal Yang?

00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:43.367
Nothing. It's just I haven't heard any
response from Sergeant Sagara in a while.

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:44.701
Do you think there might be trouble?

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:45.953
Did you hear something
from the sergeant major?

00:04:45.953 --> 00:04:47.704
No, nothing.

00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:50.541
Well, we've got our own work
to worry about. Let's go, Woo.

00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:52.000
Yes, sir.

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:08.559
Nothing here.

00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:10.561
That leaves twelve more points.

00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:28.203
Must've been a worker here, huh?

00:05:28.203 --> 00:05:32.040
Probably. Looks like
he's been dead maybe two days.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.209
This must've been their hideout, huh?

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:35.335
We don't know that for sure.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:39.464
Well, even if it was, I don't think
they'll be coming back here again.

00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:42.885
In any case, look at the guy's chest.

00:05:48.724 --> 00:05:53.854
"To the son of Bdakshon's Tiger.
Meet Hamidra at Tsim Sha Tsui."

00:05:53.854 --> 00:05:55.731
Do you know what that means, Corporal?

00:05:55.731 --> 00:05:57.900
I don't have a clue.

00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:58.901
"Tactical Division Headquarters, Command Center"

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.485
"Tactical Division Headquarters, Command Center"
Are you still unable to report to us

00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:02.946
"Tactical Division Headquarters, Command Center"
that the Venom has been spotted, Teletha?

00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:07.367
Currently, approximately 60% of
the search points have been eliminated.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.454
Please wait just a little longer,
Admiral Voda.

00:06:10.454 --> 00:06:11.705
More importantly,

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:14.458
how is the plan to stall
the heads of both governments going?

00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:16.418
We're already stalling them quite a bit.

00:06:16.418 --> 00:06:17.836
But once people suspect each other,

00:06:17.836 --> 00:06:20.672
they don't let go of
those suspicions very easily.

00:06:20.672 --> 00:06:23.425
Not to mention, that applies
even more in a situation like this,

00:06:23.425 --> 00:06:26.094
where they've already been holding
a grudge against each other for years.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.680
Naturally, we will continue
to try to negotiate with them.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:29.973
But don't expect much.

00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:32.100
We have only about
three hours left at best.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.727
Three hours?

00:06:33.727 --> 00:06:37.231
I hope to hear some good news
from you before then.

00:06:37.231 --> 00:06:38.232
That is all.

00:06:40.275 --> 00:06:43.612
Captain, Uruz 2 is on line G1.

00:06:43.612 --> 00:06:45.614
--Put her through.
--Yes, ma'am.

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:49.034
Uruz 2 to TDD HQ.

00:06:49.034 --> 00:06:51.787
I have received a report
from Corporal Yang that he discovered

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:53.288
a suspicious corpse and a message.

00:06:53.288 --> 00:06:54.039
Go on.

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:55.123
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:58.877
The body of a middle-aged man who had
been shot to death, as well as a message,

00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:01.171
were discovered at Search Point 28.

00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:03.006
The message states:

00:07:03.006 --> 00:07:08.345
"To the son of Bdakshon's Tiger.
Meet Hamidra at Tsim Sha Tsui."

00:07:08.345 --> 00:07:09.847
Furthermore, according to Intelligence,

00:07:09.847 --> 00:07:13.058
there have been two other
reports of the same message,

00:07:13.058 --> 00:07:18.480
and three reports that it is printed in the
classified ad section of local newspapers.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.481
Anything else?

00:07:19.481 --> 00:07:20.190
No, ma'am.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.693
I see. Continue with the mission.

00:07:22.693 --> 00:07:24.736
Roger. End of communication.

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:28.240
I wonder what it could possibly mean...

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.867
Speaking of Bdakshon,

00:07:29.867 --> 00:07:33.537
Lieutenant Commander Kalinin has
a strong connection to that area.

00:07:33.537 --> 00:07:34.913
Call the lieutenant commander.

00:07:34.913 --> 00:07:37.583
And then run a cryptanalysis
on the message.

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:39.001
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:40.919
I wonder what it means.

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:44.173
I don't think it's meant
as a disruption or diversion.

00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:48.552
Do you know anything about it?

00:07:48.552 --> 00:07:51.805
"Bdakshon's Tiger"
is the nickname of Majid,

00:07:51.805 --> 00:07:55.184
a legendary guerilla
commander in Helmajistan.

00:07:55.184 --> 00:07:56.852
Helmajistan?

00:07:56.852 --> 00:07:59.730
I've fought him numerous times.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:04.735
The Soviet Union sent numerous assassins
to his land in order to eliminate him,

00:08:04.735 --> 00:08:07.529
but they all failed.

00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:11.700
One of those assassins was even
a child less than eight years old.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.243
A child?

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:15.996
Majid was known for his compassion.

00:08:15.996 --> 00:08:18.874
When that child was captured,
he took the child in as his own,

00:08:18.874 --> 00:08:21.543
and gave him a new name.

00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:22.711
That name was...

00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:24.087
Kashim.

00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:24.838
Kashim...

00:08:24.838 --> 00:08:26.256
Kashim, Kashim!

00:08:26.256 --> 00:08:28.050
You sounded too friendly calling me that!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.510
You son of a bitch!

00:08:30.135 --> 00:08:31.512
Mr. Sagara...

00:08:31.512 --> 00:08:34.097
Captain, we need to
inform Sergeant Sagara.

00:08:34.097 --> 00:08:35.015
Yes.

00:08:35.015 --> 00:08:36.517
Please connect me to Uruz 2.

00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:37.643
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:37.643 --> 00:08:38.769
Go ahead.

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:43.565
TDD HQ to Uruz 2.
Please put Uruz 7 on the line.

00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:48.195
This is Uruz 2. Umm...

00:08:48.195 --> 00:08:49.988
What's the matter?

00:08:49.988 --> 00:08:54.743
I'm sorry, Uruz 7... isn't here.

00:09:18.684 --> 00:09:21.061
"Come on, have some fun
with me for a little while!"

00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:23.438
"You think I have time for that?
Just hurry up and evacuate."

00:09:23.438 --> 00:09:25.148
"Aww, don't be such a drag!"

00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:26.942
"Are you an idiot?
If you stay here, you'll die."

00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:28.402
"Hey, it's time. Let's go."

00:09:28.402 --> 00:09:31.196
"See ya! Go to hell, you stinkin' bitch!"

00:09:32.698 --> 00:09:33.907
"What did you say!?"

00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:36.827
"Right back at you!
Die, you frickin' bastards!"

00:09:36.827 --> 00:09:37.828
"Hmph!"

00:09:40.247 --> 00:09:41.999
"Oh!"

00:09:41.999 --> 00:09:44.001
"Hey, what are you doing?"

00:09:45.627 --> 00:09:49.673
"Ooh! Yeah, can't make it through
without some booze, right?"

00:09:49.673 --> 00:09:50.549
"Hmm?"

00:09:50.549 --> 00:09:51.550
"Huh?"

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:53.177
"You don't understand what I'm saying?"

00:09:53.177 --> 00:09:55.888
Are you a foreigner?

00:09:55.888 --> 00:09:57.055
Affirmative.

00:09:58.599 --> 00:10:00.017
That's a strange way of answering.

00:10:00.017 --> 00:10:01.185
Well, whatever.

00:10:01.185 --> 00:10:04.062
Hey, do you have money?

00:10:04.062 --> 00:10:05.355
A little.

00:10:06.857 --> 00:10:09.359
Then, how about it?
Are you free right now?

00:10:09.359 --> 00:10:10.277
Yes.

00:10:10.277 --> 00:10:13.238
Then would you like to
have a little fun with me?

00:10:42.893 --> 00:10:44.728
Well, how about it?!

00:10:46.396 --> 00:10:48.482
Right.

00:10:48.482 --> 00:10:51.360
Okay, let's go.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.819
What's with you?

00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:56.031
You want to do it after all,
don't you, you letch!

00:10:57.407 --> 00:10:59.368
The room's close by.

00:11:09.878 --> 00:11:12.047
Sousuke abandoned the mission?

00:11:12.047 --> 00:11:13.715
Are you serious, Speck?

00:11:13.715 --> 00:11:18.345
Yeah. I heard he got into a traffic accident,
then just wandered off somewhere.

00:11:18.345 --> 00:11:20.055
Hmm...

00:11:20.055 --> 00:11:22.057
<i>Him</i>, wandering off?

00:11:22.057 --> 00:11:24.393
Have you heard anything, First Lieutenant?

00:11:24.393 --> 00:11:26.812
Well, enough to get the general picture.

00:11:26.812 --> 00:11:29.022
But that's not enough to judge by.

00:11:29.022 --> 00:11:31.567
Lieutenant Commander Kalinin
thinks the same way.

00:11:31.567 --> 00:11:33.110
In any case,

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:36.738
we can't plan on having Sagara
and the Arbalest as part of our forces.

00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:41.201
No matter how good a mercenary he is,
he's still just seventeen.

00:11:41.201 --> 00:11:43.078
He's just a kid after all.

00:11:43.078 --> 00:11:45.163
That's got nothing to do with it!

00:11:45.163 --> 00:11:47.457
I still can't believe it.

00:11:47.457 --> 00:11:50.836
At the least, Sagara was never the kind
of guy who would do something like this.

00:11:50.836 --> 00:11:52.296
That's what I think.

00:11:52.296 --> 00:11:56.133
It's her... Yeah, Kaname Chidori.

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:58.719
Hasn't he seemed like
a really different person

00:11:58.719 --> 00:12:01.346
ever since he started
his mission to guard her?

00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:04.141
Well, now that you mention it,
I think you're right...

00:12:04.141 --> 00:12:05.934
What do you think, Roger?

00:12:06.935 --> 00:12:09.229
I don't know what Sagara's really like.

00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:14.651
But I do know that a person's true nature
doesn't change that easily.

00:12:14.651 --> 00:12:17.571
A hawk is a hawk right
until the day it dies.

00:12:17.571 --> 00:12:20.115
A hawk stays a hawk, huh?

00:12:27.289 --> 00:12:30.000
Hey, do you want yours with water?
Or on the rocks?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.001
Whatever you think's better.

00:12:31.001 --> 00:12:33.837
Oh, okay. On the rocks, then.

00:12:43.764 --> 00:12:47.226
You know, you're a lot
like this guy I know.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.482
A guy I was going out with
until just a little while ago.

00:12:59.363 --> 00:13:02.199
He was such a drag.

00:13:02.199 --> 00:13:04.451
He acted like such a big shot
in front of me,

00:13:04.451 --> 00:13:07.162
but around other people,
he'd be totally hopeless.

00:13:07.162 --> 00:13:08.664
He'd be so spineless.

00:13:08.664 --> 00:13:11.166
It pissed me off just watching him.

00:13:11.166 --> 00:13:15.504
And well, he looked
a little bit like you.

00:13:15.504 --> 00:13:18.173
He didn't scowl so much though.

00:13:18.173 --> 00:13:21.969
Hey, smile for me a little bit.

00:13:21.969 --> 00:13:26.807
I'm sure you'd look a lot better than
you do with that glum look on your face.

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:34.147
I don't know how to smile.
All I know is how to fight.

00:13:39.152 --> 00:13:43.073
You gotta be kidding me!
What would a cleaning man fight?

00:13:51.915 --> 00:13:54.084
That was too much!

00:13:54.084 --> 00:13:58.922
And the way you said it with a straight face
just made it that much more hilarious!

00:13:58.922 --> 00:13:59.923
Is that so?

00:13:59.923 --> 00:14:02.217
What? Did I hurt your feelings a little?

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:04.094
By any chance, were you actually serious?

00:14:04.094 --> 00:14:05.888
It was a joke.

00:14:22.279 --> 00:14:24.907
So, fighting cleaning man,

00:14:24.907 --> 00:14:27.034
what were you doing in a place like that?

00:14:27.034 --> 00:14:28.535
Working.

00:14:28.535 --> 00:14:30.120
Alone?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.165
No. I had comrades with me.

00:14:33.165 --> 00:14:35.459
What are they doing now?

00:14:36.502 --> 00:14:39.630
Probably still working.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.257
So you skipped out on them, huh?

00:14:42.257 --> 00:14:44.092
Affirmative.

00:14:46.178 --> 00:14:48.138
Well, that's not necessarily a bad thing.

00:14:48.138 --> 00:14:49.598
When it comes to bad stuff and tough stuff,

00:14:49.598 --> 00:14:52.476
it's best to just run away
as fast as you can.

00:14:52.476 --> 00:14:53.769
Is that right?

00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:55.604
That's right.

00:14:58.982 --> 00:15:00.234
In this world,

00:15:00.234 --> 00:15:04.363
it's the ones who take life seriously
who end up looking the fools.

00:15:05.656 --> 00:15:08.075
As long as you're with me,

00:15:08.075 --> 00:15:09.993
I can bear anything.

00:15:11.161 --> 00:15:14.665
If there's someone else
who'll do your work even if you skip out,

00:15:14.665 --> 00:15:17.417
why not just shove it on him?

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:20.504
I'm not a burden!

00:15:21.672 --> 00:15:25.759
Or, what, do you regret
skipping out on them?

00:15:25.759 --> 00:15:27.594
I don't really know.

00:15:27.594 --> 00:15:31.223
Either way, I can no longer
return to my comrades.

00:15:31.223 --> 00:15:34.393
All you did was run out on work.
You're making too big a deal of it.

00:15:34.393 --> 00:15:37.271
Just apologize to them later
and it'll be fine.

00:15:37.271 --> 00:15:38.772
No, I can't.

00:15:38.772 --> 00:15:40.983
I've already lost everyone's trust.

00:15:40.983 --> 00:15:42.526
What's so bad about that?

00:15:42.526 --> 00:15:44.653
They might say they're your comrades,

00:15:44.653 --> 00:15:47.030
but you never know when
they'll stab you in the back.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:51.368
There's no point in putting
your trust in people so easily.

00:15:51.368 --> 00:15:54.705
Even if I can't trust anyone else,
I do trust <i>you</i>.

00:15:55.956 --> 00:15:58.417
Well, when it comes
to human relationships,

00:15:58.417 --> 00:16:00.294
you should just lean on others
as much as you can,

00:16:00.294 --> 00:16:03.005
and get as much as you can out of them.

00:16:03.005 --> 00:16:05.924
And, once the relationship's not
useful anymore, just toss it.

00:16:05.924 --> 00:16:07.885
That's what it's all about.

00:16:12.014 --> 00:16:17.269
Hey, you haven't touched
your drink one bit.

00:16:17.269 --> 00:16:19.438
I've never had alcohol before.

00:16:19.438 --> 00:16:22.107
Really?

00:16:22.107 --> 00:16:24.026
I thought it would distract me.

00:16:25.861 --> 00:16:27.905
Well, whatever.

00:16:27.905 --> 00:16:30.991
Then let's save the drinking
for later and do it, okay?

00:16:30.991 --> 00:16:33.744
Forget all the bad stuff.

00:16:33.744 --> 00:16:35.746
And when you start remembering again,

00:16:35.746 --> 00:16:39.124
we'll do it again, and have some drinks.

00:16:45.756 --> 00:16:48.383
--I'll give you a good time.
--Sousuke!

00:16:48.383 --> 00:16:50.761
--I'll make you feel good.
--Sousuke!

00:16:50.761 --> 00:16:53.597
--This isn't your first time, is it?
--Sousuke.

00:16:53.597 --> 00:16:56.433
--I'll be gentle with you.
--Sousuke.

00:16:56.433 --> 00:16:59.770
--Hey... Hey...
--Sousuke! Sousuke!

00:17:04.358 --> 00:17:05.901
What was that for?

00:17:05.901 --> 00:17:07.110
I changed my mind.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:07.778
Huh?

00:17:07.778 --> 00:17:09.696
I'm not doing it.

00:17:12.115 --> 00:17:14.451
What's with you? You drag!

00:17:15.744 --> 00:17:18.080
You've been a big help.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.623
Hold it right there.

00:17:22.042 --> 00:17:24.503
You forgot something!

00:17:24.503 --> 00:17:27.130
Now get out of my sight,
you piece of trash.

00:17:44.648 --> 00:17:46.650
It's time.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:50.654
Are you ready, Teletha? Launch all M9s.

00:17:50.654 --> 00:17:52.781
Wherever the Venom shows up next,

00:17:52.781 --> 00:17:55.033
swoop in with all you've got
and take it down.

00:17:55.033 --> 00:17:57.828
However, you are forbidden
to use the Arbalest.

00:17:57.828 --> 00:18:00.163
We do not want to expose
that machine to any danger.

00:18:00.163 --> 00:18:02.165
Wait a moment, Admiral.

00:18:02.165 --> 00:18:04.835
My subordinates have not yet finalized
their countermeasures against the Venom.

00:18:04.835 --> 00:18:06.670
If I deploy them now,

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.839
I have no idea what kind
of casualties there will be.

00:18:08.839 --> 00:18:10.215
Please give me at least two more hours...

00:18:10.215 --> 00:18:13.385
No. Lord Mallory agrees as well.

00:18:13.385 --> 00:18:14.678
But...

00:18:14.678 --> 00:18:16.805
Tensions in both the Northern and
Southern Armies are at the breaking point.

00:18:16.805 --> 00:18:18.807
Not only that,
every time the Venom appears,

00:18:18.807 --> 00:18:21.143
it causes large numbers
of dead and wounded.

00:18:21.143 --> 00:18:24.688
We cannot permit any more casualties.

00:18:24.688 --> 00:18:28.358
How many more people are you going
to allow to die while you wait?

00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:29.860
Well, I...

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:33.405
I've heard that the Venom's weakness
is its short maximum operation time.

00:18:33.405 --> 00:18:35.866
We will have to strike
using that to our advantage.

00:18:35.866 --> 00:18:38.368
Have faith in your subordinates.

00:18:38.368 --> 00:18:40.746
This is what they have been
made into a top elite troop for.

00:18:42.289 --> 00:18:44.208
Is this hard for you, Teletha?

00:18:44.208 --> 00:18:48.712
But I told you. This is what
the path you are on is like.

00:18:48.712 --> 00:18:53.467
Yet you chose not to step off of it.
Am I wrong?

00:18:53.467 --> 00:18:55.469
It is just as you say.

00:18:55.469 --> 00:18:59.765
Then execute your mission quickly,
Captain Testarossa.

00:19:00.682 --> 00:19:01.892
Understood.

00:19:08.899 --> 00:19:11.068
Rise to periscope depth.

00:19:11.068 --> 00:19:13.403
Flood the underwater launch hatches.

00:19:13.403 --> 00:19:14.863
Aye, ma'am.

00:19:14.863 --> 00:19:19.326
Forward one third. Uptrim five degrees.
Rise to periscope depth.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:26.208
The search has been called off?

00:19:26.208 --> 00:19:27.209
Correct.

00:19:27.209 --> 00:19:29.795
Return to the helicopter immediately,
and board your M9.

00:19:29.795 --> 00:19:34.091
Rendezvous with Clouseau and his team
at point Echo at 0430 hours.

00:19:34.091 --> 00:19:36.176
You will receive your next orders there.

00:19:36.176 --> 00:19:37.427
Uruz 2, roger.

00:19:37.427 --> 00:19:39.513
That is all. End of communication.

00:20:01.326 --> 00:20:04.538
Begin flooding underwater launch hatches.

00:20:04.538 --> 00:20:07.457
Begin flooding underwater
launch hatches. Aye.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.047
In other words, we are out of time?

00:20:14.047 --> 00:20:17.342
Right. Leave the rest up
to the Tactical Division.

00:20:17.342 --> 00:20:18.677
Understood.

00:20:18.677 --> 00:20:19.970
Well then, goodbye.

00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:27.227
Dammit!

00:20:29.229 --> 00:20:31.815
We have reached periscope depth.
Trim is level.

00:20:31.815 --> 00:20:32.733
Stop engines.

00:20:32.733 --> 00:20:34.151
Stop engines, aye.

00:20:34.151 --> 00:20:35.485
Hatch flooding complete.

00:20:35.485 --> 00:20:36.653
Open the hatches.

00:20:36.653 --> 00:20:37.988
Open hatches, aye.

00:20:45.871 --> 00:20:49.291
Launch preparations complete, Captain.

00:20:58.717 --> 00:21:00.093
Launch all units.

00:21:00.093 --> 00:21:02.346
Aye, ma'am. Launch all units.

00:21:02.346 --> 00:21:03.597
Uruz 1, roger.

00:21:03.597 --> 00:21:05.641
All units, you have permission
to launch at will.

00:21:05.641 --> 00:21:07.017
Uruz 3, roger.

00:21:07.017 --> 00:21:08.435
Uruz 5, roger.

00:21:08.435 --> 00:21:09.561
Uruz 8, roger.

00:21:09.561 --> 00:21:11.355
Uruz 6, roger.

00:21:44.555 --> 00:21:46.723
How can people actually drink this?

00:22:03.574 --> 00:22:08.787
"To the son of Bdakshon's Tiger.
Meet Hamidra at Tsim Sha Tsui."

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.516
<i>I'm sure you're still looking</i>

00:22:29.516 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Straight ahead to tomorrow</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Just like you always have</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Just like the sunflowers</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>That bloomed on that windy hill</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>No matter how far apart we are</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>I pray that my singing will reach you</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>On nights when the tears never seem to stop</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.895
<i>I want to be the moon</i>

00:23:14.895 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>That shines through your window</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Because I believe we will meet again</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>No matter what</i>

00:23:45.217 --> 00:23:46.301
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.301 --> 00:23:48.178
<i>Time is almost up.</i>

00:23:48.178 --> 00:23:51.348
<i>A voice from the underworld echoes</i>
<i>in the heart of the deserted city.</i>

00:23:51.348 --> 00:23:54.101
<i>A flawless obituary prepared</i>
<i>by a mastermind behind the scenes.</i>

00:23:54.101 --> 00:23:56.144
<i>Who is calling me?</i>

00:23:56.144 --> 00:23:58.772
<i>Next time: "Burning Hong Kong."</i>

00:23:58.772 --> 00:24:00.440
<i>A dead man laughs at me</i>
<i>from the darkness,</i>

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:04.715
<i>beckoning me to my desolate past.</i>
